{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested at exact clean c1f73e103acc1d7049ad55ed2bdfcbd65ddd72ea (one commit over main e1ab955f; scripts/release_test.go and scripts/service_test.go, no production file). Two defects to fix before approval, both in service_test.go and the release_test.go stub. (1) service_test.go:204-206 is a dead assertion with a wrong message: an early replacement always dies on the real engine flock before it can write ready-2, so os.Stat(ready-2) is ErrNotExist in both the correct and the broken world. Proved with a double mutant (omit the exit wait and delete the non-blocking select at 199-203): the log shows two 'starting' lines and engine_already_running, line 204 passes anyway, and the test only fails 5 s later at the final awaitServiceFile with an unrelated message, 3/3 runs. The select at 199-203 is the only load-bearing assertion; delete 204-206 or assert something that distinguishes the worlds (for example exactly one 'starting' line at that instant). (2) restart-failure reasons are discarded: restart() reports errors only through http.Error(w, err.Error(), 500) and never touches t, and both stubs read it with curl --fail --silent --show-error (release_test.go:232, :249), which suppresses the body; so 'test resident did not exit after TERM; killed and reaped' (service_test.go:115) and any cmd.Start error never reach the test log on the release-test path. That contradicts the request's retained-diagnostics condition. Record the error on t inside the handler, or drop --fail and check the status in the stub. Verified: the regression TestServiceRestartWaitsForResidentExit is real and deterministic (needs no engine binary; re-executes the test binary and drives the real engine.Open flock): green 30/30 under -race and 15/15 under a 12-hog load; the omit-the-exit-wait mutant is red 5/5 plain, 20/20 -race, 15/15 loaded, failing at :201. go test ./scripts/ 26.8 s, -race 30.0 s, go vet and gofmt clean, GOOS=linux vet clean; no leaked scripts.test, serve, or /tmp/tailapps-upgrade-* after the runs. Linux CI at this head is green: CI 33952953012 (ubuntu-latest, go test and go test -race, scripts package ok 30.3 s / 32.3 s) and Release 33952953013. Informational, not blocking: removing the fake sleep shim restores the published 10 x 1 s readiness budget (was 1 s total under the shim), which is the more plausible overnight cause and has no guard; a reintroduced shim would silently re-arm it, so say so in the request or a follow-up (cost measured +5 s plain, +10-17 s on the release-assets test, well inside the 20-minute CI budget); a simulated failed start and a cmd.Start error append nothing to the log, so 'every startup/exit log' is preserved for real starts and exits only; TestServiceResidentProcess returns silently outside helper mode and reads as a passing test (t.Skip would be honest); the orphan /bin/sleep 60 residue from the serve stub drops from 3/3 runs at main to 1/10 at head and is self-limiting. Architecture: the change stays inside the release/host-lifecycle test boundary of notes/2026-08-28-tailapp-architecture.md; no production contract changes and the harness now models launchctl kickstart -k and systemctl --user restart (stop then start) more faithfully; contract preserved. Security: real os/exec ownership with Setpgid replaces a shell-written PID file and closes a genuine orphan leak; lock preservation is asserted against the real flock; all bounds finite (15 s TERM to KILL, 20 s client, 5 s readiness, 10 x 1 s published); startup/rollback, checksum, cosign identity and unit/plist checks untouched; the only new surface is a short-lived loopback httptest endpoint whose handler reads no request data, inside the note's local-user trust posture; the one defect is the discarded diagnostic in finding 2, not an authority or trust weakening. Simplification: the harness is proportionate and replaces two duplicated shell stubs, parsePID and the sleep shim without reintroducing background overlap; cuts available without weakening satisfaction are the dead assertion (finding 1) and t.Skip at 122-124.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:c3bbb430254eee05133d331f1d1684510f761f2e","head":"c1f73e103acc1d7049ad55ed2bdfcbd65ddd72ea","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:a8ae3935fa467e79502a840c9b3ba7b64d3f60d8\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:a8ae3935fa467e79502a840c9b3ba7b64d3f60d8","review_path":"reviewguard@1","stale":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:7dcade4be31cfada339d73a8e53a81b0240f521c, git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:a8ae3935fa467e79502a840c9b3ba7b64d3f60d8, git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:b1db565083965bfd361d36092be6557a48c4629f, git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:c3bbb430254eee05133d331f1d1684510f761f2e stale; retired bases: git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:235df7bfd705a08a1fdf512ecb6330c610fa1fd7, git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:3043af4d662fad21ab82c17b0065c0b9f7bca474, git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:55a40a476f7911e114b3bddee2481ada135a86df, git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:6c9dbcaa41711b1edee364b1805907cd0bf41a2b and 10 more","staleness":"artifact, promise, request stale; retired bases: git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:235df7bfd705a08a1fdf512ecb6330c610fa1fd7, git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:3043af4d662fad21ab82c17b0065c0b9f7bca474, git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:55a40a476f7911e114b3bddee2481ada135a86df, git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:6c9dbcaa41711b1edee364b1805907cd0bf41a2b and 10 more","verdict":"changes-requested"}}